      deepTheory: `<p>Facial massage is applied anatomy with a stopwatch: ten minutes, five movements, zero dragging. <b>Muscles you work over (know the map):</b> frontalis (forehead — horizontal lines), orbicularis oculi (eyes — crow's feet, feather-light only), nasalis and levators (nose/midface), orbicularis oris (mouth — perioral lines), zygomaticus mass (cheeks), masseter and temporalis (jaw/clenching — the tension reservoir), platysma (neck — downward bands), sternocleidomastoid (neck rotation). All strokes travel up and out along fibre direction, supporting skin with the resting hand; downward or random strokes stretch lax tissue the client paid you to lift.</p><p><b>The five manipulations, parameterised:</b> effleurage (flat palmar stroking, light–medium pressure, 2 min — warms tissue, spreads medium, opens and closes the sequence); petrissage (kneading, lifting, wringing of cheeks/jaw/forehead, medium pressure, 3 min — mobilises muscle, boosts perfusion, the toning workhorse); friction (small deep circles on temples, jaw attachments, brow, 2 min — releases masseter/temporalis trigger tension, headache clients notice this most); tapotement (light rhythmic tapping/hacking, 1–2 min — stimulates sluggish sallow skin, strictly avoided on thin, inflamed, rosacea or post-peel skin); vibration (fine tremor through fingertips, 1 min — sedative close that drops the nervous system into the rebooking mood). Pressure scale 1–5 calibrated at minute two; slip medium (cream/oil blend) reapplied before drag ever occurs.</p><p><b>Lymphatic reality:</b> initial lymphatics sit in the papillary dermis — feather-light pressure only (heavy pressure collapses them). Drainage pathways: forehead → pre-auricular nodes; midface → submandibular; chin/jaw → submandibular/submental; neck → supraclavicular. Sequence: clear the terminus (neck/upper chest) first, then sweep zones toward it, finishing with slow supraclavicular pumps. Indications: puffiness, post-extraction congestion, dullness, event prep; contraindications: acute infection, fever, undiagnosed lumps, uncontrolled thyroid (neck work), recent injectables per window.</p><p><b>Contraindication overlays for the whole massage:</b> skip or drastically lighten over inflamed acne, open lesions, cold sores, conjunctivitis-adjacent eye work, recent peels/laser/microneedling (per window), severe rosacea flare, Botox/filler inside practitioner-advised windows (typically 2 weeks — displacing product is a liability event). Pregnancy: side-lying or elevated positioning after the first trimester, no deep neck pressure, no essential-oil blends without obstetric-safe selection. Document pressure feedback and adaptations on the card — 'client prefers firm' today becomes your baseline tomorrow.</p>`,
      deepExtra: `<p><b>Reference — 10-minute massage map (memorise the order):</b> effleurage full face/neck 2:00 → petrissage cheeks/jaw 1:30 → petrissage forehead 1:00 → friction temples/jaw/brow 2:00 → tapotement (if suitable) 1:00 → vibration 1:00 → lymph sweeps to nodes 1:00 → closing effleurage 0:30. Set a silent timer until the rhythm is muscle memory; announce transitions softly ('warming the jaw now') so the client never startles. Draping check before hands land: chest covered, hair secured, no oil migration to linens.</p>`,
      caseStudy: { title: 'The clencher', brief: 'A client grinds her teeth, carries jaw tension headaches, and flinches at firm cheek pressure but loves deep jaw work. She is 16 weeks pregnant. Design her 10 minutes.', tasks: ['Map the safe zones vs caution zones for pregnancy + flinch response.', 'Allocate the 10 minutes across the five moves with justifications.', 'Specify positioning, oils (selection + avoidance), and pressure calibration.', 'Write the card notes that make her next visit seamless.'], debrief: 'Elevated/side-lying comfort, obstetric-safe unscented medium, pressure 2–3 with minute-2 check; friction-heavy masseter/temporalis focus (her headache reservoir), tapotement skipped, lymph light, neck gentle. Card: headache pattern, flinch zones, exact winning sequence — repeatability is luxury.' },
