      passMark: 0.7,
      deepTheory: `<p>Hair removal and makeup are high-trust, high-visibility services — errors show on the face for weeks. <b>Wax science:</b> strip wax (thin layer, removes with cloth/non-woven strip — large areas, legs, brows with precision) vs hot/hard wax (thick shrink-wrap layer, removed without strips — coarse bikini/underarm hair, sensitive faces, lower discomfort on strong hair). Hair must be 5–6 mm+ (2–3 weeks growth); too short breaks instead of pulling, too long (>12 mm) trim first to reduce pain. Contraindications absolute: broken/sunburnt skin, moles/warts, varicose veins, recent retinoids/AHA use (2–4 week windows), isotretinoin (6+ months), recent peels/laser per window, diabetes with poor healing (test-patch + GP awareness). Patch-test new waxes 24h; test temperature on your wrist then the client's jaw — burns are the commonest wax injury and entirely thermal negligence.</p><p><b>Technique parameters:</b> cleanse + light talc on perspiring skin (moisture blocks adhesion); apply with growth (strip) or against (hot wax per system), 1–2 mm thin; remove parallel to skin against growth with the other hand anchoring taut (lifting upward bruises); press immediately to dull nerve endings; never double-dip spatulas; never wax over the same strip twice (lift-off means stop, soothe, rebook). Aftercare 24–48h: no heat/sweat/fragrance/exfoliation/sun; soothing (aloe, cool compress); ingrown prevention from day 3 (gentle enzyme + non-comedogenic moisturiser, no picking — picked ingrowns scar and pigment, especially Fitzpatrick IV–VI).</p><p><b>Brow architecture, measured:</b> start (nose-wing line through inner corner), arch (nose-wing through iris outer edge, typically above the outer third), end (nose-wing through outer eye corner, not drooping below start height). Step back for symmetry every few hairs — close-up work lies. Trim only combed-up excess tips; tint (patch-tested, petroleum barrier on surrounding skin, timed to the minute, saline removal) before shaping so the true shape shows. Lamination and henna brows are chemical services with their own patch-test and timing discipline — never stack on freshly waxed skin same-day at foundation level.</p><p><b>Natural-day makeup as corrective skin optics:</b> prep (moisturiser + SPF, de-congested under-eyes with cool compress); base matched at the jawline in daylight (face is often redder than neck — match the neck); concealer one shade lighter in a triangle under eyes, exact-match on blemishes with stippling, never rubbing; colour correction (green neutralises red, peach cancels blue-dark circles, lavender lifts sallow — sheer layers, blended edges); cream blush/bronze for dry/mature (powders sit in lines); neutral eyes (matte transition + shimmer centre, tightlined upper lash for definition without harshness); brows filled in hair strokes; lips lined then filled for longevity. Strip lashes: measure, trim from outer edge, 30-second tacky wait, place centre-first, seal with liner. Hygiene: sharpened pencils, cleaned brushes (weekly minimum), no double-dipping wands, mascara decanted or disposable wands only.</p>`,
      deepExtra: `<p><b>Reference — wax incident thresholds:</b> lifting (skin removed with strip) → stop the area, cool, barrier ointment, no re-wax 2–4 weeks, document; burn → cool running water 10+ min, cover, GP if blistering, incident form + follow-up; bruise → arnica/cool, review pressure/angle technique; allergic reaction → remove, cool, document, GP pathway. Prevention beats all: temperature test, taut skin, thin layers, correct windows respected. Ingrown aftercare card given to every wax client, every time.</p>`,
      caseStudy: { title: 'The lifted brow', brief: 'You wax a bride\'s brows 2 days before the wedding; a strip lifts skin at the tail, leaving a weeping graze. She is tearful. Manage the injury and the wedding.', tasks: ['Execute the immediate protocol (stop, cool, cover, document) in order.', 'Determine the likely cause from: recent retinoid use you failed to screen, double heat, or re-waxed strip — and what each changes.', 'Write the 48-hour healing plan plus the make-up-day camouflage contingency.', 'Rebuild the screening script so this never recurs (windows, questions, test-patches).'], debrief: 'Stop, cool compress, thin barrier ointment, no makeup on broken skin, daily photo check-ins, camouflage trial on intact areas only. Cause analysis usually finds a skipped retinoid question — add medications + actives + procedures to a mandatory pre-wax checklist read aloud, with patch-test logs.' },
