      deepTheory: `<p>Single facials sell glow days; courses sell transformations — and only courses can deliver them, because skin remodels on 28-day (and slower) cycles. <b>Mild-acne course architecture (6 weekly):</b> sessions 1–2 calm + decongest (enzyme/BHA, gentle extractions of open lesions only, blue LED, barrier-support home routine issued); 3–4 deepen (layered exfoliation within tolerance, high-frequency on congested zones, niacinamide + azelaic home actives); 5–6 refine + maintain (assess grade migration, convert to monthly maintenance, photograph proof). Abort/upgrade triggers: no improvement by session 4, grade migration upward, scarring signs — GP/derm referral with a written handover, not abandonment.</p><p><b>Pigment course architecture (8–12 weekly, the patience protocol):</b> SPF discipline is treatment #1 (UV re-darkens everything — reapply counselled, hats stocked); AM vitamin C + niacinamide; weekly AHA/mandelic within Fitzpatrick-gated intensity; professional boosters (tranexamic/kojic/arbutin systems per training); strict no-pick contract (picking writes new pigment); melasma flagged as chronic management, not cure (hormonal + dermal depth + relapse risk stated upfront). Measure with same-light photos + a pigment diary (sun exposure, picking incidents, cycle correlation for melasma).</p><p><b>Ageing course architecture (6–8, honest language):</b> SPF + PM retinoid ramp (see Week 9 card) + peptide/ceramide support + red LED + massage/lymph for fluid-related ageing; vocabulary is soften/lift/glow, never erase/reverse/10-years-younger (advertising law and ethics). Dermal fillers, threads and surgery are medical lanes — your role is optimising the canvas and referring well, which builds the referral network that feeds your column.</p><p><b>Luxury tier design (24K gold, caviar, hydra-style rituals):</b> theatre + outcome in fixed choreography — double-cleanse ritual, extended massage, double-mask layering, jade/quartz or device finish, sheet-mask seal, scent + towel origami + photo moment. Price anchors: signature glow (accessible), deluxe course (core revenue), ultra-luxury event facial (margin + marketing). Boosters personalise each tier (clarifying, brightening, firming) with documented uplifts — and HydraFacial-style 7-step logic (drain, exfoliate, peel, extract, boost, light, hydrate) is the template clients already recognise from the market leaders.</p>`,
      deepExtra: `<p><b>Reference — course pricing maths:</b> per-session price × sessions = course total; offer pay-in-full (5–10% incentive) vs pay-as-you-go (higher total, lower commitment); home-care attach target 100% of course clients (results depend on it); rebook-into-maintenance rate target &gt;70% at course end. Track per-course: completion rate, grade migration, photo proof filed, maintenance conversion. A course clients do not finish is a diagnosis, pricing or experience failure — interview every dropout.</p>`,
      caseStudy: { title: 'The stalled acne course', brief: 'A grade-2 acne client shows zero improvement at session 4 of 6: same papule count, plus new picking scars. She is losing faith. Audit and rescue the course.', tasks: ['List the audit questions (compliance? picking? home routine? hormones? diet? grade migration?).', 'Decide continue / modify / refer with thresholds for each.', 'Write the honest session-4 conversation including the picking contract.', 'Redesign sessions 5–6 + maintenance for each branch of the decision.'], debrief: 'Session-4 audits separate compliance failures (fixable: picking contract, routine simplification, photo accountability) from biology (grade migration, hormonal patterns → GP pathway). Never sell sessions 5–6 blindly into failure — modify with consent or refer with handover. Documented honesty at session 4 saves the review and often the client.' },
